  "answer": "I listed the resource pools on the east cluster. The call returns every pool in the poolboy namespace on east -- four of them -- not just the one asked about, so I selected the two pools out of the full list by name.\n\nansible-automation-bootcamp-pool on east: min_available 6, max_unready 3, and it holds 11 resource handles.\n\nansible-automation-advanced-pool on east is sized differently: min_available 14 and max_unready 5 (17 resource handles).\n\nThe advanced pool keeps the larger min_available: 14 against the bootcamp pool's 6, which is 8 more ready resources on standby. If bootcamp sandboxes are slow to become ready, raising the bootcamp pool's min_available is the lever to look at. (The same-named pool on south has different sizing, but this answer is about east only.)"
